      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "iOS uses different rendering techniques, with different performance characteristics, depending on the size of each resizable area in the image:",
      "normalizedSource": "iOS uses different rendering techniques, with different performance characteristics, depending on the size of each resizable area in the image:",
      "sourceHash": "423e191af638f9f39ccd5277f0bf9cf8dc335d2cbc88c685b3fdc2214f4869de",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "For example, you can use this method to create a background image for a button with borders and corners: when the button is resized, the corners of the image remain unchanged, but the borders and center of the image expand to cover the new size.",
      "contextAfter": "If resizable areas have a width or height of 1 pixel—that is, a horizontally resizable area is 1 pixel wide, a vertically resizable area is 1 pixel tall, or the center region of the image is 1 x 1 pixel—iOS draws the image by stretching the 1-pixel region. This mode provides the fastest performance (for nonzero cap insets).",
